; Literal characters as their glyphs (change ted-latin1-glyphs, spec
; editor/screen-font, editor/literal-characters "Display, help and
; colour"), the 6 px font: a tokenised file whose lines 2-4 hold every
; character $A0-$FF (after 50 x, so that they run past the right edge),
; line 5 the no-break space ($A0) and two C1 controls ($85, $9F: the box),
; line 6 a string with an umlaut, a sharp s, an e acute, a pound sign and
; a half.  With the cursor on line 1: 90 cursor-right (scrollleft redraws
; the two right columns of every row), 90 cursor-left (scrollrite, the two
; left columns), Shift+right and Shift+left (horizpos: refresh of the whole
; screen); the rows other than the cursor row show the characters each
; time.  Nothing saved.  TED-C only: the original TED draws these
; characters from behind its font (@combos).
